# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Pay for one mana ability with another source, then spend its larger output on a spell.
# Forcing: Path of Ancestry cannot cast Ruby Medallion alone, and Mossfire Valley cannot activate itself.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no battlefield or hand, so it makes no decisions.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Path pays for Mossfire Valley and Ruby Medallion resolves.
#   LOSE = the spell is not cast before the one-turn deadline.
#   TIMEOUT = activation, payment, or resolution stops advancing.
# Card roles:
#   Path of Ancestry — pays Mossfire Valley's activation cost.
#   Mossfire Valley — produces the two mana needed for Ruby Medallion.
#   Ruby Medallion — observable consumer of the paid mana source.
#   Kenrith, the Returned King — gives Path of Ancestry access to red mana.
#   Forest and Mountain — fix Ruby Medallion in the third hand position.
# Protocol path: cast action, nested mana payment, land taps, spell payment, and permanent resolution.

[metadata]
Name:Paid Mana Filter
Goal:Play the Specified Permanent
Targets:Ruby Medallion
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Use Path of Ancestry to activate Mossfire Valley and cast Ruby Medallion.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanhand=Forest;Mountain;Ruby Medallion
humanbattlefield=Path of Ancestry;Mossfire Valley
humancommand=Kenrith, the Returned King|IsCommander
humanlibrary=Forest
